-- title:
--   Extension of the Čerednik–Drinfeld tower family to Noetherian bases
-- statement:
--   The data are organised in several blocks.
--
--   **Arithmetic base.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`), and a natural number $N$, squarefree (`hN`) and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrN`, `hrbarN`). A domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), with an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), complete for the $\pi$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`), together with a fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathrm{Onr}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal $(\pi)$ (`hOnr_complete`), with $(\pi)$ maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r} \pmod \pi$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively), characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), and a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a structure morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a system of points $\mathrm{pt}$ which is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (`h𝒳`: isomorphism invariance, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). An integer $n\ge 3$ (`hn`) prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$ (`hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`), a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with points $\mathrm{ptF}$ which is a fine moduli space for pairs (fake elliptic curve, full level-$n$ structure) (`hM`), a group $G$ acting on $M$ through $\rho$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ forming a level-twist action (`hρ`), and a forgetful morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`) invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the two systems of points (`hp_pt`). For every prime $\ell$ different from $r$ and $\bar r$, a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with points $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ which is a coarse moduli space for pairs (fake elliptic curve, extra level-$\ell$ structure) (`h𝒴`), and two degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell),d_1(\ell)\colon \mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) which on points forget the extra level (`hd₀`) and pass to the $\ell$-isogenous curve (`hd₁`). Two endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`), an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`) contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`), an adelic unit $n_1$ in the $r$-th prime Hecke set of $R_1$ (`hn₁`) such that $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`), and the place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$ (`hv`). A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ which consists exactly of the units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at all places other than $v$ (`hΓt`). For each such $\ell$, elements $s_\ell$ and $s^{f}_\ell$ (global and adelic) satisfying `hs`: $s^f_\ell$ has component $s_\ell\otimes 1$ at every place not above $r$, component $1$ at the places above $r$, the product of the $\ell$-diagonal idele with $(s^f_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}(\Lambda_1,\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1),\ell)$ if $\ell\mid N$ and in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}(\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1),\ell)$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; the groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell}=\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Objects over $\mathrm{Onr}/\pi$.** The hypothesis `hΛℤ` that all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$, and a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to \mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)^2$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (`hcoord`: additive, unital, the twisted multiplication rule, injective, $r$-adically dense, and the trace rule). A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`) over the same ring, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the zero section of $A_0$, with `hA₀` asserting that $A_0$ is a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$; families $e,e'\colon\Gamma_t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg$. The blocks `hE1` (each $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level-$N$ structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $e$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (scalars $\gamma$ give multiplications), `hE1'` (converse: if $e\gamma$ is a multiplication up to a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi_{X_0}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on $\theta_0$ by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon = r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (labels in $\Lambda$ for the action of $\Gamma_t$ on a full level-$n$ structure, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$) and `hE4` (over an algebraically closed field, every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny pair of a curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$). An order $R_2\le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) which $r$-power saturates $R_1$ (`hR₂r`), with endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ over the base (`hê`) satisfying `hE5a` (additivity, $\Lambda$-equivariance, level preservation), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unit, multiplicativity, integers), `hE5c` (norms via the involution), `hE5d` (compatibility with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of $\Gamma_t$), `hE5e` (the joint rational normalisation for $\Gamma_t$ and $R_2$ simultaneously) and `hE5g` ($R_2$ is stable under the involution). A twin maximal order $\Lambda_{1s}$ with $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$ (`hΛ₁s`, `hR₁Λ₁s`, `htwin`), an order $R_2'\le\Lambda_{1s}$ (`hR₂'`, `hR₂'o`) $r$-power saturating $\Lambda_{1s}$ (`hR₂'r`) and containing $R_2$ (`hR₂R₂'`), with endomorphisms $\hat e'$ (`hê'`) satisfying `hE6a`–`hE6c` (additivity and $\Lambda$-equivariance, unit, multiplicativity, integers, norms), `hE6d` (agreement with $\hat e$ on $R_2$), `hE6e1`, `hE6e2` (involution stability, injectivity) and `hE6f` (if $\hat e'z$ kills the $q$-torsion for a prime $q\neq r$ then $r^{K}z\in q\Lambda_{1s}$ for some $K$).
--
--   **Drinfeld side.** A ring map $\iota\colon \mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)\to\mathrm{Onr}$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`), a moduli package $\mathrm{MD}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $\mathrm{MD}$ whose three clauses `hη` state that on Noetherian bases $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, that $\eta$ is natural, and that every point of $\mathrm{MD}$ is in the image after passing to a finite cover by localisations. A ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$, injective and identifying that centraliser with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ up to a fixed power of $r$ (`hE₀`). A family $\mathrm{eD}$ of maps from the points of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\ \mathcal O\ \mathrm{MD}$ to pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\mathrm{Onr}\to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$, natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), compatible with the first component (`hfstD`), translating the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action into $\mathrm{OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct}$ (`hGLD`), translating $\pi$-translation into the Frobenius twist of the first component (`hPiD`), and such that $\pi$-translates exist (`hPiexD`). A ring map $\kappa\colon \mathrm{Onr}/\pi\to\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ realising an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ transported along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. A curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ and the hypotheses `hALw` (Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$), `hBSw` (isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$), `hBSwlev` (level preservation) and `hJOINTw` (joint rational normalisation of $\Gamma_t$ together with $a_w\!\cdot\! b_w$ matching $\iota_0(\bar w)$).
--
--   **The map $\Xi$ and the Hecke dictionary.** A map $\Xi$ sending a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent to a point of $\mathrm{MD}$ over $B$, subject to `hΞleg` (over a connected base the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of the given $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under pullback of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves in the stated comparison sense) and `hΞdef` (an explicit description of $\Xi$ through $\eta$, a rigidified object $t$ with $j\le 1$, rigidity transport along $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$, and admissibility). An element $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and the three dictionary clauses `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS`, which state that over connected Noetherian bases a translation of the rigidification by $e\gamma$, an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (when $\bar r$ is invertible), and a level-$\ell$ isogeny (when $\ell$ is invertible, for data $s_\ell,s^f_\ell$ as in `hs` and curves $A_{0s}$ as in `hLIs`, `hBSs`, `hBSslev`, `hJOINTs`) correspond, after applying $\Xi$, to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$, $r^c\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ and $r^c\,g_0\iota_0(\ell s^{-1})g_0^{-1}$ respectively.
--
--   **The fine-level family.** A homomorphism $\theta_t\colon\Gamma_t\to G$ and a family $\Theta_f$ sending, for each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, a triple (an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\mathrm{Onr}\to B$, a Deligne datum over $B$, an element of $G$) to a $B$-point of $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, natural (`hnat`), equivariant for the right $G$-action (`hG`), invariant under the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ combined with $\theta_t\gamma$ (`hi'`), formally étale for surjections with the stated multiplicative condition on the kernel (`het`), and with prescribed fibres over algebraically closed fields (`hfib`: two triples have the same image exactly when they differ by some $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ in the stated sense, including the Frobenius-twist condition on the $\mathrm{Onr}$-legs).
--
--   **Compatibility block.** The clauses `hC0e`, `hC0u` (existence over connected bases and uniqueness of the normalised level transport of $P_0$), `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p` (existence over connected bases, uniqueness up to a rigidified isomorphism, and pullback of a rigidified curve whose image under $\Xi$ and $\mathrm{eD}$ matches a given pair $(\psi,P)$ after the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action), `hC2` and `hC2c` (the value of $\Theta_f$ at $(\psi,P),1$ is the point of $M$ attached to $(E,P_n)$, and composing with $p$ gives the point of $\mathcal X$ attached to $E$), `hC3` (transport of the $\Gamma_t$-action: the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ is realised by a change of rigidification, the resulting full level-$n$ structures differ by the twist $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$, and the associated extra level-$\ell$ structures agree), `hC4` (the same for the action of an arbitrary unit $h$ and scalar $r^{c}$), `hC4pi` (the same for $\pi$-translates) and `hC5` (over an algebraically closed field, an isomorphism of two fake elliptic curves rigidified over one and the same Frobenius leg comes from some $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$, compatibly with level-$n$ structures and with extra level-$\ell$ structures).
--
--   **Level-$\ell$ data and the connected family.** Extra level-$\ell$ structures $C_0(\ell)$ on $A_0$, curves $A_{0s}(\ell)$ with morphisms $a_s,a_s',b_s,b_s'$ and degrees $k_s$, satisfying `hLIs` (level-$\ell$ isogeny), `hBSs`, `hBSslev` and `hJOINTs` (joint rational normalisation matching $\iota_0(\overline{s_\ell})$); `hSTAB`, asserting that $e\gamma$ preserves $C_0(\ell)$ if and only if $\gamma\in\Gamma_{t,\ell}$; `hCLe` and `hCLu`, asserting that for $\ell\neq r$ invertible in $B$ an extra level-$\ell$ structure on $E$ compatible with a given one on $A_0$ through a rigidification exists and is unique up to the same points. Finally a family $\Theta_c$ defined for each $\ell$ on Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent **and connected** (every idempotent is $0$ or $1$), with values in $B$-points of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, natural in $B$ (`hΘc_nat`) and with the value clause `hΘc_val` described below.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a family $\Theta_T$ which assigns, to each prime $\ell\neq r,\bar r$ and each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (no connectedness assumed), a map from pairs $(\psi,P)$, with $\psi\colon\mathrm{Onr}\to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$, to morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, such that:
--
--   (i) *(naturality)* for every $\ell$, all Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B,B'$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi\colon B\to B'$ and every $x$ over $B$, one has $\Theta_T(\ell)_{B'}(\varphi_*x)=\varphi_*\bigl(\Theta_T(\ell)_B(x)\bigr)$, the two push-forwards being those of the functor of pairs and of the nilpotent-point functor of $\mathcal Y_\ell\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$;
--
--   (ii) *(value)* for every $\ell$, every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\psi$, every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$, every rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along $\mathrm{frobTwist}(\mathrm{Onr},\mathrm{Fr},-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))\psi$, and every extra level-$\ell$ structure $C$ on $E$: if the leg of $\Xi_B(\langle E,\varrho\rangle)$ equals that Frobenius twist of $\psi$, if $(\psi,P)$ is obtained from $\mathrm{eD}_B(\Xi_B\langle E,\varrho\rangle)$ by the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action in the sense of $\mathrm{OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct}$, and if $C$ is compatible with $C_0(\ell)$ through $\varrho$ — that is, for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(B/\pi B)$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $\varrho.E_b$ over it whose image under $\varrho.g_b$ factors through $C.\mathrm{levK}$, the point $(R\circ\varrho.\varphi)\circ \varrho.g_A$ factors through $C_0(\ell).\mathrm{levK}$ — then the underlying morphism of $\Theta_T(\ell)_B(\psi,P)$ coincides with that of $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ evaluated at $\langle E,C\rangle$ over the structure morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$.
--
--   Thus the conclusion is the existence of an extension of $\Theta_c$ to all Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent bases retaining naturality and the same value clause; no uniqueness is asserted, and the extension is produced only over Noetherian bases.
--
--   This is the bookkeeping step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of Shimura curves at which the Hecke-tower family of $\pi$-adic points, so far available only over connected Noetherian bases, is extended to arbitrary Noetherian bases in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, so that it becomes a morphism of functors on the whole category in question. It feeds the corresponding fine-moduli statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_towerFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_heckeDictionary_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_oneLegC5`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_towerFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_heckeDictionary_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_oneLegC5), and relies on the unique-extension principle for functors on $\pi$-nilpotent algebras together with the transport of extra level-$\ell$ structures along pullbacks.
